  "findings": [
    "All four held-out action errors are resolved and improve approximately tenfold over the two-panel initialization. Eight-panel ordered response remains 1.45\u20131.63 times more accurate on all four.",
    "Learned endpoint and zero-readout endpoint differences are below teacher uncertainty. The excellent endpoint is predominantly supplied by classical defect correction, not demonstrated learned benefit.",
    "Combined physical endpoint/action loss is numerically dominated by action rows: training endpoint MSE is ~3.46e-25 versus action MSE~1.31e-14 after fitting; validation similarly differs by ~12 orders. It is not balanced evidence of two tasks.",
    "Two source directions on one diagnostic parent cannot establish operator accuracy, state coverage, long-time stability, mesh transfer, or superiority.",
    "The data design has numerical rank25/40. Positive ridge makes the exact conditional minimizer unique, while weakly excited source-time columns and data-only column scaling degrade the augmented system. More optimizer iterations or a learned encoder do not address this first.",
    "Full-map JVP agrees closely with an independent variational diagnostic and finite differences converge quadratically, but the derivative teacher has no refined uncertainty and no certificate.",
    "The cubic FD residual auditor certifies finite-grid upper bounds at h=.04 (~1.17e-7 fitted, ~1.37e-7 Strang) without checking a requested tolerance. This is a whole-panel reconstruction bound, not the observed ~1e-12 endpoint error.",
    "Uncached fitted inference still constructs forty spatial columns even though fixed state/time coefficients reduce to five scalar branch weights. A streamed evaluation can preserve the exact represented map while removing unnecessary design materialization.",
    "Single-call action timings suggest a comparison worth measuring, but repeated matched-tolerance tests, proper warmup, a truly uncached P-only endpoint baseline and complete path/audit/fallback accounting are absent."
  ],
