    "acceptance": [
      "All declared bounded CPU checks pass without skip; actual native CPU verification for the updated source remains separate from cloud checks.",
      "Original ridge objective, parent weights and penalty are unchanged. Compare against an independent original-coordinate augmented least-squares solution; numerical gradient/gap and baseline nonregression must pass the predeclared implementation tolerances.",
      "Show equilibration reduces artificial augmented conditioning on near-null fixtures while retaining the reported original design rank and all columns; no silent truncation or new regularizer.",
      "Streaming primal, action linearity, affine design and complete JVP agree with the unstreamed graph across nonzero readouts and varied input/physics/time cases using declared FP64 tolerances.",
      "Replayed metrics retain parent/task/horizon/direction identities and unchanged references; threshold or ranking changes are reported, never retroactively used to recategorize job2930.",
      "Measured speed is descriptive until randomized repeated complete-call timing meets a prospectively frozen common accuracy contract. Native CPU replay success still cannot promote B STOP or GPU readiness.",
      "A later scientific R7 protocol must specify fresh bounded state/physics/time/source coverage, per-task tolerances and reference margins, strong classical controls, selection splits and total-cost accounting before generating evidence."
    ],
    "changes": [
      "Add objective-preserving augmented-column equilibration, scales=sqrt(weighted_column_norm^2+lambda), retaining the transformed ridge penalty and independent original-coordinate diagnostics.",
      "Keep training designs but evaluate production inference by contracting 8 state/time features into each of 5 branch coefficients before spatial assembly; validate full-map derivatives including input, physics and time.",
      "Add an explicitly uncached classical P-only response-corrected endpoint baseline and retain cached zero-head attribution as a separate row.",
      "Instrument complete path/autograd work where trustworthy; otherwise retain unknown counts and use complete-call timings. Record derivative and auditor costs separately.",
      "Retain old artifact/source hashes, emit a new implementation identity and fresh replay root, preserve both versions, and use train-only scaling/fitting plus the same fixed validation selection menu.",
      "Derive and test an analytic leading-error commutator control on independent tiny static matrix and time-varying examples before any scientific comparison; do not infer a fourth-order or stiff-stability theorem from cancellation.",
      "Prepare, but do not yet promote, a future fixed-state five-coefficient oracle and source-holdout protocol to distinguish representation limitations from coefficient conditioning."
    ],
